WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.001
A few numbers capture DS-1000.

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:05.538
It offers a thousand problems over seven libraries,

00:00:05.618 --> 00:00:09.769
drawn from four hundred fifty-one unique
StackOverflow posts.

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:14.555
The best model reaches only forty-three point three
percent accuracy.

00:00:14.635 --> 00:00:19.133
The evaluation is highly reliable: among all
solutions it accepts,

00:00:19.213 --> 00:00:22.740
just one point eight percent are actually incorrect,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.248
and only about half a percent of rejected ones are
truly correct.

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:30.994
And with a hundred forty words per problem on average,

00:00:31.074 --> 00:00:34.670
its contexts are far richer than comparable datasets.
